// SIGNS
text SignMessage1_part1{
    "1) The game's mechanics reflect GEN 9\n"
    "where possible; overworld mechanics\l"
    "are the main exception.\p"

    "2) Moves & learnsets are mostly vanilla.\n"
    "Move PP may be reduced (e.g. 5 PP Mimic)\l"
    "to suit puzzle design.\p"

    "3) Battle RNG has been disabled.\n"
    "Outcomes are deterministic (0% or 100%)\l"
    "with Assist as sole exception.\p"

    "4) There are no hidden items.\p"

    "5) EXP gain from battling has been\n"
    "disabled.\p"

    "6) Any Pokémon could have custom IVs or\n"
    "EVs, including wild Pokémon.\p"

    "Keep reading?"
}

text SignMessage1_part2{
    "7) Your party is fully healed each time\n"
    "you beat a trainer.\p"

    "8) You'll never get softlocked.\n"
    "The game has an anti-softlock system\l"
    "to undo any mistake you could make.\l"
    "This may have side effects (such as\l"
    "healing your party) to prevent gaining\l"
    "an advantage via the system.\p"

    "9) There are QOL features that further\n"
    "reduce any need for save states, like\l"
    "the option to restore a pre-damaged\l"
    "state after losing.\p"

    "They're strictly QOL and not required to\n"
    "solve any of the puzzles."

    // "9) There are QOL features to further\n"
    // "reduce the need for save states:\l"
    // "- You can run from trainers.\l"
    // "- Wild battles can be forfeited.\l"
    // "- Used items may return after battle.\l"
    // "- Pre-damaged states can be restored.\l"
    // "- Losing far from the respawn lets you\l"
    // "   warp back to the battle area.\p"
    // "None of these features are required to\n"
    // "solve any of the puzzles."
}

